course: dictionary
lesson: 10966
title: Clues from a shared past
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words name things you may never have seen. The sentence around the word often explains what the thing is. «Many peoples kept laws in memory, speeches and objects, like the Haudenosaunee Great Law of Peace, remembered with belts of shell beads called wampum.» The word "called" tells you the author is naming the thing, and "shell beads" tells you what it is made from.
explain: Now read the second sentence: «the Haudenosaunee Great Law of Peace was remembered with wampum belts.» Belts that help people remember a law are not just decorations, so wampum belts must carry meaning. Put your clues together: wampum is shell beads, and belts made from them were used to keep important information. Then check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence.
explain: Always ask: what job does this word do in the sentence? In these sentences, wampum does the job of a memory or a record. A dictionary can confirm your idea and add more detail.
fact: Wampum means small beads made from white and purple shells.
fact: Native American peoples of eastern North America strung wampum together or wove it into belts.
fact: «Wampum belts» were used to record agreements, tell histories and mark important promises between nations.
fact: Later, European settlers also used wampum as a kind of money, so the word can mean shell money.
fact: The old US slang meaning, money in general, is now rare and can sound disrespectful, so avoid using it.
exercise: What were «wampum belts» used for? | *Recording agreements and marking important promises | Lighting up dark rooms | Making bread for the village | Keeping cows safe on the farm
exercise: «The Great Law of Peace was remembered with belts of shell beads called wampum.» What is wampum? | A type of cloth for summer clothes | *Small beads made from shells, strung or woven together | A kind of tall tree | A fast wooden boat
exercise: Ella says wampum is just a fancy word for money. Why is she only partly right? | Wampum is a kind of food | *Settlers used it as money later, but it was also used to record agreements and tell histories | Money and wampum are exactly the same thing in every way | Wampum has never been used as money by anyone
test: Which two words in «Many peoples kept laws in memory, speeches and objects» show that laws were kept without writing? | *in memory and in speeches and objects | memory and writing | laws and peoples | kept and laws
test: «Somali clans used xeer, a law kept by elders.» What does this sentence teach you about how laws were kept? | Laws were never remembered | Laws were always written on paper | Laws were kept in a museum | *Laws could be kept by people, such as elders, without writing
exam: Read «wampum belts» and «shell beads» in the sentences, then explain in one sentence what wampum is and what it was used for. | Wampum is a kind of cloth used for clothes | Wampum is a tool for digging in the earth | Wampum is a sweet food eaten at feasts | *Wampum is shell beads, strung or woven into belts to record agreements and histories
